{
  "task": "Write Python 3 function solve(rows). First apply an audit filter to the ORIGINAL input positions, indexed from zero: omit positions whose index modulo 5 equals 3, except always retain the last input position. Rotate the retained rows LEFT by 3 positions modulo the retained length (empty stays empty). Apply the following rules to that transformed list: Aggregate rows [key, amount, void]. Ignore void rows and amounts whose absolute value is below 9; sum signed amounts by key. Return sorted [key,total] lists, dropping zero totals.\nReturn the requested value, without printing. Inputs follow the types specified. Do not mutate the input. Standard library is allowed.",
  "specification": "First apply an audit filter to the ORIGINAL input positions, indexed from zero: omit positions whose index modulo 5 equals 3, except always retain the last input position. Rotate the retained rows LEFT by 3 positions modulo the retained length (empty stays empty). Apply the following rules to that transformed list: Aggregate rows [key, amount, void]. Ignore void rows and amounts whose absolute value is below 9; sum signed amounts by key. Return sorted [key,total] lists, dropping zero totals.",
  "reference": "def solve(rows):\n d={}\n for key,v,void in rows:\n  if not void and abs(v)>=9: d[key]=d.get(key,0)+v\n return [[k,v] for k,v in sorted(d.items()) if v!=0]\n_core_solve=solve\ndef solve(rows):\n filtered=[row for i,row in enumerate(rows) if i%5!=3 or i==len(rows)-1]\n if filtered:\n  shift=3%len(filtered)\n  filtered=filtered[shift:]+filtered[:shift]\n return _core_solve(filtered)",
  "mutation": "def solve(rows):\n d={}\n for key,v,void in rows:\n  if not void and abs(v)>9: d[key]=d.get(key,0)+v\n return [[k,v] for k,v in sorted(d.items()) if v!=0]\n_core_solve=solve\ndef solve(rows):\n filtered=[row for i,row in enumerate(rows) if i%5!=3 or i==len(rows)-1]\n if filtered:\n  shift=3%len(filtered)\n  filtered=filtered[shift:]+filtered[:shift]\n return _core_solve(filtered)",
